# =============================================================================
#  Internal-only material -- NOT published
# =============================================================================
#  The public repository carries the code scaffolding only. Research findings,
#  infrastructure specifics, cost figures and project planning stay private
#  until the work is published.
#
#  Note that /docs is where the project's reasoning lives. If you are reading
#  this in the public repository and a comment refers to a document you cannot
#  find, that is why -- ask the project manager.
/docs/
/Deliverables/
/notebooks/
*.pdf

# Data and artefacts live in S3, never in the repo.
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING: an unanchored `data/` also matches
# src/rdd/data/, which would silently exclude the entire data pipeline from the
# repository and break CI on the first push.
/data/
/runs/
/logs/
*.pt
*.onnx
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.jpg
*.png
!docs/**/*.png

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Local overrides -- may contain account-specific values
infra/config.local.sh
.env

# Never commit credentials
*.pem
*.key
credentials
.aws/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs
docs/